  "body": "QUESTIONABLE / PROJECTION. MAINLINE-040 common account complete; filed 037b incorporated (200 F cure, compliant-core/free-edge model, 30.341397 scarf). Reoptimizes 120 radius/weather/joining/pad/venting combinations with coating, service, 100 kg systems, weather pressure and both complete wind cases.\n\nR30 needs least optimism for ISA and optimistic weather: gamma+Q. With the retained floor, full two-factor endpoint payloads at R20/R30 are 1,296.561/6,100.222 kg ISA; R30 optimistic is 1,964.195 kg. Both-weather does not close in the stated ranges. The table gives every least set, necessary coefficients, film weight and signed payload.\n\nMarginal face-tuple floats receive E credit from 033, not a binding compression-strength improvement; fixed-E interpretation is explicit. Service 30-50 kg sits inside 100 kg; extra-service alternatives are costed. Light pads fail 70 kn. Unvented cells remain mechanically open.\n\nCoating 0.20 kg/m2 is assumed, bracketed 0.10-0.40. Free-edge minimum factor is about 1.07; cure, edge model, hardpoints and combined weather/thermal qualification remain open. The prior rigid 037 screen is preserved as a comparison and does not pass the retained-floor account.\n\n48,476 primary checks pass; modulus and cavity audits pass. Installed SF unknown. One report; stop/file, no successor.",
